            <ArticleTitle>Childhood obesity: the challenges for nurses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16, 18-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7748/ncyp2014.03.26.2.16.e398</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity is one of the biggest challenges facing UK children's nurses today. However, it is a problem borne of many causes and requiring multi-level interventions. It is important for children's nurses to understand the underlying causes of patients' weight issues and how to engage with young people and their families to achieve a healthy weight. Nurses must be willing to engage in policy debates about whether the UK governments are doing enough to combat what has been termed 'the obesity epidemic'.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
